# playpick cell: mode=walk boss=skyward spec=druid:feral style=auto
# size=25 difficulty=heroic view=844x390,touch save=carried (behaves as
# fresh, #273 -- carried never actually carries across separate playbot
# invocations because the dev-server port is derived from the process pid).
# `boss=skyward` is a coverage label only: evening steers at no boss, the
# walk starts at the door same as any other.
#
# A fresh/carried save only opens Bonegrinder 10-normal by default, so
# #b=marrow&s=25&h=1 unlocks the whole chain up to 25-heroic before backing
# out to a real RAID -> WALK IN at the door (direction.md's 2026-09-26
# driver-lesson recipe), rather than landing on the invite's own single-fight
# "visiting" framing.
#
# What no session has done before: `style=auto` has only ever been run
# inside a standalone raid pull, a daily pull, or a battleground -- never
# inside `evening`/mode=walk, and never on a melee class at all (every prior
# auto session was a caster: mage:frost, druid:feral(desktop, fell back to
# good), druid:restoration, paladin:holy). direction.md's 2026-09-26 note
# already read scripts/playbot.ts and confirmed `auto` never steers -- it
# releases movement every tick and lets the toggle cast for it -- which cost
# a restoration druid every heal on a battleground because nothing held
# still in range. `cross()` steers every corridor itself regardless of style,
# so the corridors should behave the same as any other evening; the open
# question is what a *melee* dps that never approaches anything does inside
# an actual boss room, on real 25-heroic numbers, across more than one fight.
open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
tap back
tap raid
tap next
tap class:druid:feral
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start

evening auto 200 5
state
shot end
says
bill
